# 4.8 Building Panel 7 – Running Pods

---

# Objective

The seventh panel created for the Enterprise Platform Overview dashboard displays the number of healthy `auth-service` Pods currently running within the Kubernetes cluster.

Unlike previous panels, which focused on application performance and resource utilization, this panel provides visibility into the Kubernetes deployment itself.

It allows engineers to quickly verify whether the expected number of application replicas are running and available to receive traffic.

This panel answers the operational question:

> **How many healthy application Pods are currently serving traffic?**

---

# Why This Metric Matters

One of Kubernetes' primary responsibilities is maintaining the desired number of application replicas.

If Pods fail because of:

- Node failures
- Image pull errors
- CrashLoopBackOff
- Out Of Memory (OOM)
- Failed deployments
- Readiness failures

the number of running Pods decreases.

Monitoring the number of healthy Pods provides immediate visibility into deployment health.

This panel becomes particularly valuable during:

- Rolling Deployments
- Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) scaling
- Node maintenance
- Cluster upgrades
- Production incidents
- Load testing

